  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday Night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1158 AM CDT Mon Jun 29 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge will be centered over Middle TN on Wednesday\nand this will likely be the peak of the heat wave with highs in\nthe mid 90s to right around 100. Afternoon heat index values will\nget as warm as 112. Overnight lows Tuesday night through Wednesday\nnight will be very warm in the mid to upper 70s with some areas\npossibly staying in the lower 80s. The upper level ridge will\nstart to drift to the east mid to late week and will slowly start\nto flatten. The cooling will be very limited with highs staying \nin the mid to upper 90s through Friday and very hot heat index \nvalues. It looks like we will see some cooling over the July 4th \nweekend but not a ton, it will still be very hot and you should \nplan for the heat if you have outdoor plans. Highs over the \nweekend will remain in the low to mid 90s with heat index values \nas warm as 107. Additional cooling is expected Monday as a short \nwave trough pushes into the Great Lakes. This will continue to \nflatten the ridge and drop our highs back into the upper 80s to \nlower 90s. As the ridge pushes east late week we will see low \nchances for popup showers and thunderstorms mainly during the \nafternoons and early evenings. These low thunderstorm chances look\nto continue into the holiday weekend.",
